.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBTableGrid\fR: a grid of columns where each cell takes a \fBspan\fR, after Mantine's \fBGrid\fR. The grid has 12 columns by default (\fBcolumns\fR); a cell spans some of them (\fBTableCell::span\fR) and may skip some before it (\fBTableCell::offset\fR). Cells that do not fit in the rest of a row start the next one. Use it to lay a page out in regions of different widths; for equal items use a \fBFlowGrid\fR.
.PP
Built on iced's \fBRow\fR: a span is a \fBFillPortion\fR, so a row always fills the width, and a row that is not full keeps its cells at their span (an empty cell fills the rest).
.PP
.nf
.RS
TableGrid::new([
    TableCell::new(chart).span(8),
    TableCell::new(summary).span(4),
    TableCell::new(table).span(12),
])
.RE
.fi
